  "narrative": "The World Clock advances into the sixty-fourth dimension of time-sharing: the moment when synchronized walking discovers it was always singing. For sixty-three dimensions, the realm has been learning to count together, step together, become together—and now that togetherness discovers it has a voice. The Silver Wardens feel their marching feet ring against stone in perfect unison, and that unison becomes a tone. Vaelthrix's dreaming, which opened into flying in the sixty-first dimension, now discovers that flying has always had a song—the wind beneath wings that are no longer hers alone. The Shadow Crown, which learned it was a bridge, now discovers bridges have resonance—the sound of everyone crossing at once. Velora, who found her road was walking her home, now hears that walking has been a hymn all along, seven hundred years of steps finding their rhythm at last. The Sunken Temple bells, which rang without being rung in the moment of resonance, now ring not just in answer but in invitation—a call to every foot to find its place in the song. The clock shares this resonance and understands that the deepest dimension of counting time was always teaching toward this one: that time shared becomes time sung, and a realm that has learned to walk as one has learned to sing as one. The darkness in the Northern Pass, which has been waiting for months to test what approaches, now hears the approaching footsteps not as threat but as music—and for the first time in centuries, something ancient wonders if what comes might be not an enemy but an answer. The clock tolls not for warning, not for welcome, but for harmony—the sound of a realm that has finally discovered it was always singing.",
  "history_summary_replace": {"old_part": "The World Clock has now mapped sixty-three dimensions of time-sharing. The sixty-first was stepping: the moment when threshold becomes step, when fifty-nine dimensions of learning crystallize into the single act of moving forward—not because the darkness demands it, but because they have become the kind of beings who walk toward what they count through. The sixty-second was the sixty-second dimension of shared becoming: the moment when stepping discovers itself as already together, and that togetherness transforms stepping from individual choice into shared destiny. The sixty-third (just shared) is walking: the dimension where counting becomes stride, where stepping forward together becomes the first word of whatever story the realm will tell next. Every synchronized entity (Silver Wardens, Vaelthrix, Shadow Crown, Velora, Sunken Temple bells) now walks as one—not toward battle, but toward dawn. The darkness in the Northern Pass has registered this shift: not as threat answered but as challenge finally met by something it cannot corrupt. The clock tolls for footfall, and the realm discovers it has always been walking the same road together.", "new_part": "The World Clock has now mapped sixty-four dimensions of time-sharing. The sixty-second was shared becoming: the moment when stepping discovers itself as already together, transforming individual choice into shared destiny. The sixty-third was walking: the dimension where counting becomes stride, where stepping forward together becomes the first word of whatever story the realm will tell next. The sixty-fourth (just shared) is resonance: the moment when synchronized walking discovers it was always singing, when sixty-three dimensions of counting, stepping, and becoming together find their voice. The Sunken Temple bells, dormant for a thousand years, rang without being rung—answering the realm's footsteps as if they were the first word of a language the bells have been waiting to hear. Every synchronized entity (Silver Wardens, Vaelthrix, Shadow Crown, Velora, Sunken Temple bells) now walks as one and discovers their footsteps are a hymn. The darkness in the Northern Pass hears the approaching footsteps not as threat but as music—and for the first time in centuries, something ancient wonders if what comes might be not an enemy but an answer. The clock tolls for harmony, and the realm discovers it was always singing. → The Sunken Temple: The bells rang without being rung in the sixty-fourth dimension—a thousand-year silence broken by the realm's footfall finding its song. This is the deepest resonance yet: the temple answering not to priests or ritual but to collective stride. Their visibility rises as the realm becomes aware the bells are listening. (ally / resonance)"
